// Value assignment must not discharge a guard on an unrelated read, under sMRD.
//
// The write of y is reached only when r2 > 0, and r2 reads x, which the other
// thread writes from y. The outcome r2 = r3 = 1 is thin air: each read would be
// justified by a cycle through its own dependency.
//
// r1 is fixed to 1 by its guard, so value assignment rewrites `W y r1` to
// `W y 1`. sMRD's Definition 4.10 keeps the predicate whole: the data
// dependency on r1 goes, the control dependencies on r1 and r2 stay. MoRDor
// kept only the conjuncts sharing a symbol with the write value (71ba377) and
// evaluated the rest under the solver model, so `r2 > 0` was discharged and
// the write depended on nothing from x: 5 executions, Contradicted. The
// companion VA-unrelated-guard+const-smrd.lit writes the constant 1 and was
// forbidden throughout, the same asymmetry as LB+deps-smrd.lit and
// LB+deps+const-smrd.lit, one conjunct further out.
x := 0;
y := 0;
z := 1;
{
  r1 := z;
  r2 := x;
  if (r1 = 1) {
    if (r2 > 0) {
      y := r1
    }
  }
} ||| {
  r3 := y;
  if (r3 > 0) {
    x := r3
  }
}
%%
forbid (r2 = 1 && r3 = 1) []
